    "babble": {
      "word": "BABBLE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To utter words indistinctly or unintelligibly; to utter inarticulate sounds; as a child babbles.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To talk incoherently; to utter unmeaning words.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To talk much; to chatter; to prate.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To make a continuous murmuring noise, as shallow water running over stones. In every babbling he finds a friend. Wordsworth. noisy after having found a good scent.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To utter in an indistinct or incoherent way; to repeat,as words, in a childish way without understanding. These [words] he used to babble in all companies. Arbuthnot.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To disclose by too free talk, as a secret.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "Idle talk; senseless prattle; gabble; twaddle. \"This is mere moral babble.\" Milton.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Inarticulate speech; constant or confused murmur. The babble of our young children. Darwin. The babble of the stream. Tennyson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
